{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Kentucky girl are you [D]lonesome tonight
[D]Kentucky girl do you [G]miss me
[G]Does that old moon shine on the [D]bluegrass as bright
[D]As it did on the night you first [G]kissed me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]In a valley neath the [D]mountain so high
[D]The sweetest place in all the [G]world
[G]In a cabin with the [D]vines on the door
[D]Is where I met my Kentucky [G]girl
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm far away from old Kentucky tonight
And the blue-eyed girl that I love so
But I'm heading home in the silvery moonlight
With open arms she waits I know
{end_of_chorus}
